==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Indo-European|ḱiesdʰ-|to drive away; to go away|lang=la}}. Cognates include Sanskrit {{term|सेधति|tr=sedhati||to drive, chase away|lang=sa}} and Avestan {{term||tr=siizdat̰||will chase away|lang=ae}}{{rfscript|Avestan}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈkeː.do/|lang=la}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|cedo|cēdō|cedere|cēdere|cessi|cessī|cessum|cessum}}

# {{intransitive|lang=la}} I [[go]], [[move]], [[proceed]], [[go along]], [[move]] along.
# {{intransitive|lang=la}} I [[result]], [[turn out]], [[happen]].
# {{intransitive|lang=la}} I [[withdraw]], [[depart]], [[retire]], go away from.
## {{intransitive|military|lang=la}} I withdraw, [[fall back]], [[give up]] my post.
# {{intransitive|lang=la}} I [[disappear]], [[pass away]], [[vanish]].
# {{intransitive|with dative|lang=la}} I [[cede]], [[give in]] or [[yield]] (to), [[step aside]] (for), [[give way]] (to).
## {{intransitive|lang=la}} I am [[inferior]] to, yield to in rank.
# {{transitive|lang=la}} I [[concede]], give up, [[grant]], [[surrender]], [[yield]].
# {{intransitive|with dative or in +acc.|lang=la}} I [[fall]] (to) (as a possession); [[accrue]] or [[come]] (to).
# {{intransitive|with in +acc.|lang=la}} I [[become]], [[turn into]], be or become the [[equivalent]] of.

